{"title":"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47affecc93688552c8eca8bc13560d52b4cc28a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, there is a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a65fe5f396d8c182d88144d00e26156435e0743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> for every distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bda82ee8212aa2c03bc02d76fc28a5bda8412ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proof by induction.  For n=2, the proof is trivial, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/2966c70b0c8f338b8b96b534974a395e4e497ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = (1,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies the condition.  Assume now that there is such a set S of n elements, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff2024b147ef40e1e48aa65e5f844e82823cd1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2,...a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"11\" /> which satisfy the condition.  The key is to note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bfc92ed339bc34839bb12105a6a5f2e11223b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=a_1a_2...a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" />, then if we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74bc5e73a25d6aa9cf8ea191fd2716947a0e451f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i=a_i + km$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb780fd19aa86d0cdd8bb5df87ffe68a1af0ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, where k is a positive integer, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db50d9660050618bcf2c97b0661667a4c51b955c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\mid b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb0cd134be124348281cc3edff91351c5010c25c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i - b_j = a_i - a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ff9fc6efc900ec14dc876c84f4fdcaf2c8253d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_i - b_j)^2 = (a_i - a_j)^2 \\mid a_ia_j \\mid b_ib_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"260\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38f01fcf19e444307fc6d479873805fa9f599c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n+1}=m +km$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />.   Consider the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d41fac741471f03a11f07641b32efca2d0b6963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = (b_1,b_2,...,b_n,b_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />. To finish the proof, we simply need to choose a k such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3fa83217c8f0f82a6d7da591529c0d6d65013047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_{n+1}-b_i)^2 \\mid b_{n+1}b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb780fd19aa86d0cdd8bb5df87ffe68a1af0ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f3976453294bef8306a051d033f98e18a180a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_{n+1}-b_i)^2 = (m-a_i)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"19\" />, simply choose k so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee4208331bcf419a3181720f9f930574093f99e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1 = (m-a_1)^2(m-a_2)^2...(m-a_n)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"311\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO\" title=\"1998 USAMO\">1998 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;t